            {"day": "Wed", "mins": 45, "topic": "Azure Policy, initiatives, resource locks and tags",
             "learn": "Policy definitions, initiatives, assignments, effects (Deny, Audit, Modify, DeployIfNotExists), compliance and remediation; lock types; tag governance. Read the [Azure Policy overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/policy/overview). Optional: [Lock your resources](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/management/lock-resources).",
             "do": "Assign the built-in 'Allowed locations' (Central India + South India) and 'Require a tag on resource groups' (costCenter) policies at subscription scope; prove both with non-compliant creates (expect RequestDisallowedByPolicy). Add a ReadOnly lock to an RG holding a storage account and observe what breaks (e.g., listing keys). Then remove the tag-policy assignment (or add `costCenter` to `new-lab.sh`) so later labs aren't blocked. Done when: 2 denials + lock behaviour are documented in `w07/policy.md` and no lab script fails on the tag rule."},
            {"day": "Fri", "mins": 45, "topic": "Management groups, subscriptions, budgets, cost alerts and Advisor",
             "learn": "Management group hierarchy, moving resources between resource groups, budgets with action groups, cost alerts, Azure Advisor recommendations, and policy exemptions: Allowed locations will block Foundry models offered only outside India, so before AI W25 (12 Apr) you exempt that one resource group instead of deleting the policy. Read the [Management groups overview](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/governance/management-groups/overview). Optional: [Cost alerts](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/costs/cost-mgt-alerts-monitor-usage-spending).",
             "do": "Create management group `mg-learning`, move your subscription under it, and re-assign 'Allowed locations' there (check inheritance in the compliance view). Create an RG-scoped budget that triggers an action-group email at 80%. Record 3 Advisor recommendations (or why there are none). Move a storage account between RGs with `az resource move` and compare resource IDs. Write the `az policy exemption create` command you'll need in April. Done when: MG tree, budget, Advisor notes, move output and the exemption command are committed."},
            {"day": "Sat", "mins": 60, "topic": "LAB: AZ-104 Lab 02a - custom roles and RBAC at scale",
             "learn": "Custom roles (Actions, NotActions, DataActions, AssignableScopes) assigned at management-group scope. Do the official [Lab 02a - Manage subscriptions and RBAC](https://microsoftlearning.github.io/AZ-104-MicrosoftAzureAdministrator/Instructions/Labs/LAB_02a_Manage_Subscriptions_and_RBAC_Entra.html). Optional, if time remains: the Modify-tag + remediation task in [Lab 02b - Manage governance via Azure Policy](https://microsoftlearning.github.io/AZ-104-MicrosoftAzureAdministrator/Instructions/Labs/LAB_02b-Manage_Governance_via_Azure_Policy.html).",
             "do": "Before starting, write your own `w07/custom-role.json` for a 'VM operator' (start, stop and restart VMs; read resource groups), then compare it with the lab's approach. Complete Lab 02a (management group, custom role, assignment); add Lab 02b's Modify + remediation task if time remains. Repeat one assignment in Az PowerShell in Cloud Shell (`New-AzRoleAssignment -SignInName <upn> -RoleDefinitionName Reader -ResourceGroupName <rg>`). Clean up the custom role, lab assignments and RGs. Done when: Lab 02a is done, the PowerShell assignment was listed and `custom-role.json` is committed."},
